Z||000000||pHoOl||12-17-2000||03:05 PM||||What are your guys thoughts on under side neon?  If it's on a fiero, is that fiero a ricer?  <P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.gvsuphool.homestead.com/files/pHoOl_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Seanh||12-17-2000||03:30 PM||||I have Aqua undercar neon on my Fiero. I am also going to have EL blue penstriping and interior neon.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/transsig.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://www.kdsi.net/~sean" TARGET=_blank>Sean's Fiero Page</A><BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8 Auto<BR>Going on to 3.4 in Jan.<BR><I>"It's always in the last place you look." Of course it is. Why would you keep looking after you've found it? Do people do this? Who and where are they?</I>||||reg||1
Z||000002||DaRkLoRD||12-17-2000||03:49 PM||||I think neon looks cool as long as it's not overdone.. in stereos (sub boxes, amp enclosures etc) it looks awesome, and under the car looks good at night. but I couldn't stand having neons inside the car where I could see them.... it'd be too distracting I think.<P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||3
Z||000003||pHoOl||12-17-2000||03:52 PM||||Yeah, i've always thought that it looks cool under.  thinking about doing it in the summer with JC's kit that is 150, but i'm not sure if i can't find a better way to spend the money.<P>later<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.gvsuphool.homestead.com/files/pHoOl_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Philphine||12-17-2000||04:42 PM||||if  i thought it would be durable enough, i like to try using some of those neon speaker rings sort of right around or just behind my brake disks so that the light shined through my wheels. but they would probaly have to move with the suspension to get the desired effect and i'm sure they'd get rattled to death. <P>still considering something along those lines where the light comes through the wheels.<p>[This message has been edited by Philphine (edited 12-17-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||fldevel||12-17-2000||05:46 PM||||i have neons under my car ..but be warned .. theres really nowhare to put them and there illegal if you can see the "bulb" itself ..i ended up cutting arches in my kicker panels and mounting them in there ..you might be able to squeeze  2 4 footers in those lil groves on either side of the gas tank but i wouldent recomend it for obveous reasons ||||reg||1
Z||000006||FieroLisa||12-17-2000||07:14 PM||||The couple fieros I've seen with underside neons looked hideous since you could see the bulbs. I think the idea of it is great- but when you see the car pass and you have this awful neon rod hangin out, it ruins it. I was going to put purple under the coupe but decided against it. One of my friends put greenish yellow under his GT and on the back tube he put black electrical tape so you couldn't see it so well but it still glowed from the front..make sense?<BR><P>------------------<BR>Lisa<BR>86 gold 4 speed GT<BR>86 gold 5 speed SC (For Sale)<BR>Columbus, OH/Greensboro NC<BR>*Lots of New Pics!* <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/</A>||||reg||1
Z||000007||pHoOl||12-17-2000||09:14 PM||||JC Whitney has some sort of thing that i remember seeing that makes light glow from the inside of the wheels just like you're describing.  Check out their site and see if you can find it.  <P>As for the neon, i thought that in MI if you have any light under there it's illegal.  Might differ by state.  Any lawyers that would know?<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.gvsuphool.homestead.com/files/pHoOl_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
