Z||000009||FieroJoe||12-17-2000||10:05 PM||||Yeah I heard too that the light underneath is illegal in MI, but then again that was from a kid that actually had some neon under his car, and he could have been trying to make himself look tough.<P>------------------<BR>FieroJoe<BR>c311t@yahoo.com<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000010||Seanh||12-17-2000||10:14 PM||||According to State (Nebraska) Law, you cant be able to see the "bulb" itself when your eye level with the bottem of the car, it must be recessed. I however have it mounted so that if you stick you head down there and look, you can see the bulb. I never get pulled over for it, but I have heard of others who have been. I also have a red neon tag frame I got pulled over for. So me, being an a$$hole, got my screw driver out and turned it around backwards so it is backlit. It looks really good. I saw somthing funny tonight on a ricer, they were valve stem caps that blinked. Probally just use a hearing aid battery. But they were different, never seen that before. Check out <A HREF="http://www.varad.com" TARGET=_blank>Varad</A> They have some pretty awesome automotive lights. I have the interior neon, but havent installed it yet. I also have a blue EL Scanner, ELS600 Series mounted under my rearview mirror. They look really cool and not to ricy.||||reg||1
Z||000011||My7Fieros||12-17-2000||11:19 PM||||<B>YES</B> ...but go ahead and do it if you want, its your car Uncle Ben  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000012||SloPonti||12-18-2000||12:19 AM||||i have the under car neon light set! i use the three foot tubes in the front and back and four foot tubes on the side of the car! you cannot see the tubes at all unless you get down and look underneath the car. i also have them under the dash to and they are only visable if you stick your head under the dash. i also have neon lighting rods in the motor compartment so when i go to car shows i can show off the motor a little better!<BR> <IMG SRC="http://members.aol.com/sloponti/fiero1.jpg"> ||||reg||10
Z||000013||GT Bastard||12-18-2000||12:35 AM||||I wouldn't call it rice... I think it's more "pimp-daddy."  I chuckle every time I see a car with neon, because it's always some punk-assed gangster wannabee driving.  But I don't think neon lights are inherently bad.  I just haven't seen it done tastefully.<BR>||||reg||10
Z||000014||Standard||12-18-2000||01:09 AM||||I've been thinking about putting some small blue neon's up in the footwells of my GT, to replace the interior lights.  One of my friends has an S-10, and he used some small tubes on the interior.  Looks really good with a grey interior..<P>------------------<BR>Mike -<BR>Black 86.5 GT 5 Spd, 153,000 miles and some busted up ground f/x  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/redface.gif"> <BR>Red 84 Sport Coupe - winter donut maker    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/asthanos.gif"> ||||reg||1
