Z||000016||Tigger||12-18-2000||09:02 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Philphine:<BR><B>if  i thought it would be durable enough, i like to try using some of those neon speaker rings sort of right around or just behind my brake disks so that the light shined through my wheels.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Have you guys seen the lighted glowing tire valve caps?  At speed they create a ring of light around your wheels.  Come in several colors.  Never thought about putting them on any of my cars, but that would give a similar effect.<P>Not sure, but didn't undercar neon originated in Miami?  I think it's pretty cool when done right (can't see the bulbs).  I'm afraid Michigan roads would do a number on them.<P><P>------------------<BR>T-T-F-N, Tah Tah For Now!<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tiggerblue2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000017||bHooper||12-18-2000||11:21 AM||||i used to sell aftermarket auto electronics, including neon, and here is my take...<P>1) if you can see the tube, then it is done wrong.<BR>2) if there isn't a even spread of light under the car, then it is done wrong.<P>the neon, should spread evenly underneath the car, creating a "hovering" effect.  to do this properly, you must use the right length of tube, as well as having the right amount of power going to them (voltage is the big secret with tubes, more the better).<P>on the GT, the lights can be mounted between the coolant pipes and ground effects.  the one draw back to this, is when putting the car on a lift for service... the tech needs to be real carefull.<P>it's kinda interesting to see this topic on something that i hadn't seen as "popular" in a few years.  in the early '90's you would see cars with neon something, everywhere... now it is the rare car that has neon.<P>and yes, the trend started in South Florida.<P>hoop<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000018||Tone007||12-18-2000||11:32 AM||||I used to drive around with two 2-foot flourescent blacklights mounted between the headrests of my seats and in the back window of my Cavalier, Sunbird, and Firebird.  Not only did this look cool, but it made everything glow crazy (white stuff especially.)  Got lots of looks, believe me.  Completely illegal in NJ, but I was only pulled over once in the 2 or 3 years I had them, when the cop told me they weren't legal I just played dumb and he let me go.  I was just lucky, I guess.||||reg||14
